; `scaly run` of a program that calls a routine defined nowhere in the run --
; neither in the program, nor in a package object, nor in the tool's own image
; (a standard-library routine newer than the tool is one). The JIT's stub for
; it ends the run where it is called, naming the symbol (exit 25); until
; 2026-11-22 it answered zero and the run went on as if nothing had happened.
function '_Z5ghostv'() returns int extern
print "before"
let g '_Z5ghostv'()
print "after `g`"
